 Zones:**\n- Dreadlands [zone=75]\n- Lake of Ill Omen [zone=73]\n- Old Sebilis [zone=89]\n- Swamp of No Hope [zone=74]\n- Thundercrest Isles [zone=279]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a Sarnak adherent [npc=3979]\n- a bloodgill goblin [npc=3960]\n- a tundra yeti [npc=4106]\n- froglok ilis shaman [npc=4579]\n- froglok krup knight [npc=4573]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Dragons of Norrath Cultural Equipment [quest=3056]\n**Era:** | !Dragons of Norrath\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- Beastlord\n- Monk\n- Necromancer\n- Shadowknight\n- Shaman\n- Warrior\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- Iksar\nEntered: Mon Feb 21 13:26:49 2005\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Click here** [quest=3056] for an overview of cultural armor introduced with Dragons of Norrath.\n_Find Sieeva Koan in East Cabilis, location +851, -439._\nYou say, 'Hail, Sieeva Koan'\nSieeva Koan says 'Hello, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Returning home from conquests abroad, I hope. It fills me with pride to see there are still Iksar willing to venture out into Norrath and crusade for our empire once again. Too many of us have holed up in this city, dreaming of the [glory] days of the Iksar empire.'\nYou say, 'Glory days?'\nSieeva Koan says 'From what I have heard things were much different then, our military more refined, our craftsmanship more detailed. I have been studying the writings in the ruins of old Cabilis. They are helping me piece together the [techniques] of our ancestors.'\nYou say, 'What techniques?'\nSieeva Koan says 'From what I have learned, our craftsmanship has regressed over the years. In fact, I've uncovered some armor patterns and symbol patterns within the ruins that put our current designs to shame. Would you be interested in learning the [cultural armor patterns] and [cultural symbol patterns]? They will take time to master, but if you are patient, they will serve you well.'\nYou say, 'I am interested in learning the cultural armor patterns'\nSieeva Koan says 'Excellent. To make you a pattern book I will need a patch of bloodgill scales for the cover, a scroll for the pages, a bloodstone ring for the clasp, and a cat's eye agate to grind down and make a salve which will protect and preserve the finished product. I have heard these items can be found in the Swamp of No Hope and the Lake of Ill Omen. Bring them to me and the pattern book shall be yours.'\nYou say, 'What about the cultural symbol patterns?'\nSieeva Koan says 'You're interested in the cultural symbol patterns I see. I can give you the symbol patterns but I will need you to run a few tasks for me before I can give them to you. What do you say; would you like to run a few short [tasks] for me?'\nYou say, 'What tasks?'\nSieeva Koan says 'I have four tasks that need to be completed. The first is an adventure into [Lake of Ill Omen] where you will collect some shields for my shield collection. The next you will be tasked with venturing into the [Dreadlands] where you will confront any clans that are preventing us from doing buisness. The third task leads you into [Sebilis] where you will learn if there is any weakness in Trakanon's army. The last task will lead you onto an adventure into [Thundercrest] where you will learn about the creatures that inhabit the area.'\n**Items to return for the Ancestral Iksar Armor book:**\nBloodgill Scales (dropped by bloodgill goblins)\nA Scroll (dropped by sarnak adherants)\nBloodstone Ring (dropped by random low-to-midlevel mobs)\nCats Eye Agate (dropped and vendorbought)\n**Task given for the Journeyman's Book: Tales of Sieeva**\n1) Kill 20 Goblin Warriors in the Lake of Ill Omen\n2) Loot four Green Goblin Skins\n3) Return skins to Sieeva\n4) Kill 10 Pond Sturgeons (Firiona Vie / Lake of Ill Omen zone line)\n5) Loot one Pondfish Spine\n6) Return spine to Sieeva\n_Receive Journeyman's Book._\n**Task given for Expert's Book: Protect the Operation**\n1) Kill 50 Tundra Yeti in the Dreadlands\n2) Loot 20 Frosty Datura\n3) Return Frosty Daturas to Sieeva\n4) Kill five Dracnid silkmistresses\n5) Loot one Drachnid Silk\n6) Return Drachnid Silk to Sieeva\n_Receive Expert's Book._\n**Task given for Master's Book: Scouting the Enemy**\n1) Kill any 80 Froglok Krups in Sebilis\n2) Loot 40 Wax Flowers\n3) Return four Wax Flowers to Sieeva\n4) Kill five Froglok Ilis Shaman\n5) Loot one Nodding Blue Lilly\n6) Deliver Nodding Blue Lily to Sieeva _Receive Master's Book._\n**Task given for Grandmaster's Book:**\n1) Kill 120 Thundercrest Isle creatures (must have 'Isle' in name)\n2) Loot 80 Fractured Drake Claws\n3) Return Drake Claws to Sieeva\n4) ?\n5) ?\n6) ?\n_Receive Grandmaster's Book._\n**Types of Armor**\n_Mistwoven - Necromancer_\n_Shadowrise - Beastlord, Monk_\n_Trooper - Shadowknight, Warrior_\n_Twoscale - Shaman_\n- Elaborate Mistwoven Armband [item=38887]\n- Elaborate Mistwoven Boots [item=38886]\n- Elaborate Mistwoven Breeches [item=38885]\n- Elaborate Mistwoven Cap [item=38884]\n- Elaborate Mistwoven Gloves [item=38883]\n- Elaborate Mistwoven Robes [item=38882]\n- Elaborate Mistwoven Sleeves [item=38881]\n- Elaborate Shadowrise Armband [item=38549]\n- Elaborate Shadowrise Boots [item=38888]\n- Elaborate Shadowrise Cuirass [item=37761]\n- Elaborate Shadowrise Gloves [item=38889]\n- Elaborate Shadowrise Greaves [item=38890]\n- Elaborate Shadowrise Helm [item=38891]\n- Elaborate Shadowrise Sleeves [item=38313]\n- Elaborate Trooper Armband [item=38551]\n- Elaborate Trooper Boots [item=38557]\n- Elaborate Trooper Cuirass [item=38552]\n- Elaborate Trooper Gloves [item=38553]\n- Elaborate Trooper Greaves [item=38554]\n- Elaborate Trooper Helm [item=38555]\n- Elaborate Trooper Sleeves [item=38556]\n- Elaborate Twoscale Armband [item=38860]\n- Elaborate Twoscale Boots [item=38861]\n- Elaborate Twoscale Cuirass [item=64812]\n- Elaborate Twoscale Gloves [item=38872]\n- Elaborate Twoscale Greaves [item=38834]\n- Elaborate Twoscale Helm [item=38835]\n- Elaborate T